        <h4>China</h4>
        <p>Long, blunt-tipped chopsticks (often 25-30cm), typically bamboo or plastic. Used for shared dishes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="country-card">
        <div class="flag">🇯🇵</div>
        <h4>Japan</h4>
        <p>Shorter, tapered tips (21-24cm). Often lacquered wood. Sized differently for men, women, and children.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="country-card">
        <div class="flag">🇰🇷</div>
        <h4>Korea</h4>
        <p>Metal chopsticks (often stainless steel), flat and slender. Used alongside a spoon for rice.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="country-card">
        <div class="flag">🇻🇳</div>
        <h4>Vietnam</h4>
        <p>Long, blunt chopsticks similar to Chinese style, often made from bamboo or lacquered wood.</p>
      </div>
